---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import WordDrum from '../components/WordDrum.astro';
import DrumPause from '../components/DrumPause.astro';
import InstallBar from '../components/InstallBar.astro';
import Passage from '../components/Passage.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import sorterShot from '../assets/sorter.png';
import { OVERVIEW } from '../components/features-data';
import { svg } from '../components/docs/icons';
---

<Base
	title="Rays: Free Download Manager for Mac with AI File Sorting"
	description="Free, open-source download manager for Mac. Downloads as fast as your line allows, survives dropped connections, and sorts every file with on-device AI."
>
	<div class="page">
		<main id="main" class="column" data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-meta="title:Rays: free download manager for Mac">
			<SiteNav />

			<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
				<div class="headline">
				<h1 id="hero-title">
					<span class="sr-only">File management for everything you download.</span>
					<span aria-hidden="true" class="lead">File management for</span>
					<WordDrum />
				</h1>
				<DrumPause />
				</div>
				<Panel />
				<p class="sub">Rays downloads from your browser, Terminal, AI assistants and Hugging Face at full line speed, in queues that run on your schedule. Then every file lands in a folder that fits, sorted by AI that never leaves your Mac. Free.</p>
				<InstallBar />
			</section>

			<figure class="shot">
					<Image
						src={sorterShot}
						alt="The Rays Sorter tab: on-device AI is ready, new files sort after 10 seconds, files are renamed from their content, and the Documents and Downloads folders are watched."
						widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
						sizes="(max-width: 899px) calc(100vw - 32px), 640px"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption>The Sorter tab in Rays: the folders it watches and when it files new arrivals.</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<Passage title="A download isn't done at the last byte" id="why">
				<p>
					Files reach your Mac from everywhere now: browsers, Terminal, AI assistants, cloud buckets, model and
					dataset hubs. They all land in one folder and stay there, under names like <code>download (3).zip</code>.
				</p>
				<p>
					It's done when the file is where you'll look for it. Rays does both halves.
				</p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Everything Rays does today" id="features">
				<p>Five groups. Each one opens its docs page.</p>
				<div class="overview">
					{OVERVIEW.map((g) => (
						<section aria-labelledby={`ov-${g.id}`}>
							<h3 id={`ov-${g.id}`}>
								<a href={g.href}>
									<Fragment set:html={svg(g.icon, 22)} />
									<span class="name">{g.title}</span>
								</a>
							</h3>
							<p>{g.summary}</p>
							<ul>
								{g.short.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
							</ul>
						</section>
					))}
				</div>
				<p class="more"><a href="/features/">See all features</a></p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Paste a wall of links" id="downloads">
				<p>One per line, comma-separated, or a whole CSV. Rays finds every one.</p>
				<figure class="paste">
					<pre aria-label="An example of pasted text with three links in it"><code>From the release thread:
<mark>https://huggingface.co/openai-community/gpt2/resolve/main/model.safetensors</mark>
"rays", "mac", <mark>https://github.com/a6n-ai/rays/releases/latest/download/Rays.dmg</mark>
installer two: <mark>https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.0/python-3.13.0-macos11.pkg</mark> (signed)</code></pre>
					<figcaption><span>3 links</span> picked out of the text, ready to download</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<dl class="features">
					<div>
						<dt>Every connection pulls its weight</dt>
						<dd>
							Files of 32 MB or more start on 4 connections and double, up to 16, but only while each step makes the file faster.
							A part that finishes early takes half of the biggest part left, and a slow connection is replaced, so
							nothing idles at the finish line.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Remembers difficult servers</dt>
						<dd>
							When a server pushes back, Rays remembers it for 7 days and asks for fewer connections next time. A
							server that cannot send parts gets one steady stream.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Drops don't cost you</dt>
						<dd>
							A connection that drops mid-file reconnects at once and continues from its last saved byte. A server
							that goes quiet gets up to 5 retries, from 2 seconds apart to a minute. Pause, quit, come back: nothing
							downloads twice.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Cloud buckets too</dt>
						<dd>
							Browse Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2 or any S3-compatible bucket and download with the same engine.
							Secret keys stay in your Keychain.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>You set the pace</dt>
						<dd>Cap the speed, and choose how many files download at once, from 1 to 10.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Safe names, always</dt>
						<dd>Rays cleans the name the server suggests, so a file can never land outside your folder.</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Rays measures, then adds connections" id="engine">
				<p>
					More connections don't always mean faster. On a line one connection already fills, extra connections just
					fight each other, and your file arrives later. So Rays measures: a connection stays only while it makes the
					download at least 10% faster, and Rays steps back down when more stop helping.
				</p>
				<figure class="ramp" data-ramp>
					<ol>
						<li style="--n:4;--speed:0.25"><b>4</b><span class="lanes" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="rate">8 MB/s</span></li>
						<li style="--n:8;--speed:0.5"><b>8</b><span class="lanes" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="rate">16 MB/s <em>kept, +100%</em></span></li>
						<li style="--n:16;--speed:1"><b>16</b><span class="lanes" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="rate">32 MB/s <em>kept, +100%</em></span></li>
					</ol>
					<figcaption>
						Connections per step, on a server that caps each one at 2 MB/s. On a line one connection already fills, the
						first step brings nothing, and Rays goes back down.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<dl class="stats" aria-label="Benchmark results">
					<div>
						<dt>31<span> MB/s</span></dt>
						<dd>the full speed of a 250 Mbit/s line, for a 2 GB file over HTTPS</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>12&times;</dt>
						<dd>faster than aria2 on its default settings, when the server caps each connection at 2 MB/s</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>43<span> MB/s</span></dt>
						<dd>while the server drops connections at random. aria2's defaults give up</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>1.8<span> GB/s</span></dt>
						<dd>for a 2 GB file from a local server, faster than curl on one stream</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<dl class="features">
					<div>
						<dt>Not one wasted request</dt>
						<dd>The first request, the one that reads the file's size, keeps downloading instead of being thrown away.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Crash-safe</dt>
						<dd>
							Rays saves its plan before it reserves disk space and counts only bytes already on disk. After a crash it
							resumes from the last saved byte.
						</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<p class="more"><a href="/docs/engine/#benchmarks">See every benchmark, and rerun them yourself</a></p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Your Downloads folder, finally tidy" id="sorting">
				<p>
					Rays watches it, and any folder you add. A few seconds after a file
					arrives, it moves into a folder that fits, like Installers, Archives, Images or Work.
				</p>
				<p>Rays can even rename files from what is inside them, or keep every original name. Your call.</p>
				<ol class="flow" aria-label="How a file gets sorted">
					<li><span class="step">Arrives</span><code>download (3).pdf</code><p>lands in Downloads, or any folder you add</p></li>
					<li><span class="step">Waits</span><code>10 s to 1 hour</code><p>you choose how long, so you can open it or move it yourself first</p></li>
					<li><span class="step">Reads</span><code>Apple on-device AI</code><p>Apple Intelligence reads what is inside, on your Mac, never in the cloud</p></li>
					<li><span class="step">Files</span><code>Work/Invoice March.pdf</code><p>into a folder that fits, with a clear name</p></li>
				</ol>
				<dl class="features">
					<div>
						<dt>Your folders, your rules</dt>
						<dd>Send any category where you want it, for example Work to <code>~/Documents/Work</code>.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Works without AI too</dt>
						<dd>Disk images go to Installers and screenshots to Images even on a Mac without Apple Intelligence.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Tidy what's already there</dt>
						<dd>New files sort themselves. For the ones that were there first, run <code>dl sort FOLDER --all</code>.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>See every move</dt>
						<dd>The Recent tab lists the latest moves. Click one to open the file, or show it in Finder.</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Models from Hugging Face" id="models">
				<p>
					Search Hugging Face from Rays. Trending models show as cards with a type colour and icon, and you can filter
					by Text, Vision, Image, Audio or Embeddings.
				</p>
				<p>Download the one quantization you need, or save it straight into LM Studio's models folder.</p>
				<dl class="features">
					<div>
						<dt>Verify what you downloaded</dt>
						<dd>Rays checks each file's size and SHA-256 offline, and downloads again only the files that are bad.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Same engine</dt>
						<dd>A model file downloads like any other, with pause, resume and your speed limit.</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<p class="more"><a href="/docs/app/models/">Read about models</a></p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Queues that run on your schedule" id="queues">
				<p>
					Main is the default queue. Add more, each with its own icon, colour, speed limit and number of files at a
					time. Then say when each one runs.
				</p>
				<ol class="flow" aria-label="How a scheduled queue runs">
					<li><span class="step">Starts</span><code>start time</code><p>once, every day or on chosen days, with an optional stop time</p></li>
					<li><span class="step">Checks</span><code>conditions</code><p>Wi-Fi only (not a hotspot), charging, or the Mac idle</p></li>
					<li><span class="step">Runs</span><code>its own limits</code><p>the queue's speed limit and files at a time</p></li>
					<li><span class="step">Finishes</span><code>your choice</code><p>play a sound, quit, sleep, lock, shut down, or run a command</p></li>
				</ol>
				<dl class="features">
					<div>
						<dt>Wake the Mac</dt>
						<dd>Optional. Rays can wake a sleeping Mac for a scheduled queue. It asks for your admin password once.</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Activity history</dt>
						<dd>A history of what your queues have done.</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<p>Or send a download to the best time of night: Rays learns when your connection is usually fastest, from your downloads and a speed test. <a href="/docs/app/speed/">Speed test and best time</a>.</p>
				<p class="more"><a href="/docs/app/queues/">Read about queues and schedules</a></p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Your files stay on your Mac." id="private" big>
				<p>Sorting runs on Apple's on-device model. Nothing is uploaded, and there is no account to make.</p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Terminal, AI assistants and your browser" id="anywhere">
				<p>
					Rays comes with the <a href="/docs/dl/"><code>dl</code> command</a>, so you can download and sort from Terminal, or let AI assistants do it over <a href="/docs/mcp/">MCP</a>: they can add downloads to a queue, start and stop queues, and verify a model. The
					Rays extension for <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/mgepiogdappnhmohefhalmeppkfciail">Chrome</a> and <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/addon/rays@a6n.ai/">Firefox</a> sends links to Rays with a right-click.
				</p>
				<a class="browsers" href="/docs/app/browser/">
					{['chrome', 'brave', 'edge', 'firefox', 'zen'].map((b) => (
						<img src={`/browsers/${b}.svg`} alt="" width="22" height="22" loading="lazy" />
					))}
					<span class="label">Get the extension</span>
				</a>
				<p>Rays lives in your menu bar and Dock with progress at a glance, and keeps downloading after you close the window.</p>
				<p>New version out? Click Update. Rays installs it and reopens.</p>
			</Passage>

			<Passage title="Open source, made by a6n" id="a6n">
				<p>
					Rays is open source under the AGPL-3.0 licence. The code, issues and releases live on{' '}
					<a href="https://github.com/a6n-ai/rays">GitHub</a>.
				</p>
			</Passage>

			<Faq />

			<Newsletter />

			<footer class="foot">
				<a class="slide" href="https://github.com/a6n-ai/rays">GitHub</a>
				<span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<a class="slide" href="/docs/">Docs</a>
				<a class="slide" href="/features/">Features</a>
				<a class="slide" href="/docs/app/browser/">Browser extension</a>
				<a class="slide" href="/releases/">Release notes</a>
				<a class="slide" href="/support/">Support</a>
				<a class="slide" href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
				<a class="slide" href="/terms/">Terms</a>
				<a class="slide" href="https://a6n.ai">a6n.ai</a>
				<span>AGPL-3.0</span>
			</footer>
		</main>
	</div>
</Base>

<script>
	// The ramp starts collapsed and draws once it is on screen. Without JS, or under reduced motion, it shows at rest.
	const ramp = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-ramp]');
	if (ramp && !matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
		ramp.classList.add('idle');
		new IntersectionObserver((entries, seen) => {
			if (entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) {
				ramp.classList.remove('idle');
				seen.disconnect();
			}
		}, { threshold: 0.4 }).observe(ramp);
	}
</script>

<style>
	/* The underline draws under the label only, not under the browser icons; the icons hop in turn. */
	.browsers .label {
		background: linear-gradient(currentColor, currentColor) left bottom / 0 1px no-repeat;
		padding-bottom: 2px;
		transition: background-size 220ms var(--ease-out);
	}
	.browsers:hover .label,
	.browsers:focus-visible .label {
		background-size: 100% 1px;
	}
	.browsers img {
		transition: translate 220ms var(--ease-out);
	}
	.browsers:hover img,
	.browsers:focus-visible img {
		translate: 0 -2px;
	}
	.browsers img:nth-child(2) { transition-delay: 30ms; }
	.browsers img:nth-child(3) { transition-delay: 60ms; }
	.browsers img:nth-child(4) { transition-delay: 90ms; }
	.browsers img:nth-child(5) { transition-delay: 120ms; }
	.browsers {
		justify-self: start;
		width: fit-content;
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 8px;
		margin-bottom: 0;
		color: var(--ink);
		font-size: var(--t-small);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.browsers span {
		margin-left: 6px;
	}
	.shot {
		margin: 0 0 8px;
		max-width: 40rem;
	}
	.shot img {
		width: 100%;
		filter: drop-shadow(0 24px 32px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.28));
	}
	:global(:root[data-theme='light']) .shot img {
		filter: drop-shadow(0 20px 28px rgb(60 40 20 / 0.22));
	}
	.shot figcaption {
		margin-top: 12px;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: var(--t-small);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.more a {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
	}
	.hero {
		display: grid;
		gap: 22px;
		min-height: calc(100svh - 96px);
		align-content: center;
		padding-block: 48px;
	}
	/* One 40rem column. The pause button sits just past the drum's right edge, on the line it controls. */
	.headline {
		--fs: clamp(2.25rem, 4.4vw, 4.25rem);
		position: relative;
		max-width: 40rem;
		font-size: var(--fs);
	}
	/* Two lines: the lead, then the drum at the same size. Sized so the lead fills the 40rem hero column. */
	h1 {
		margin: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: flex-start;
		font: 500 1em / 1.05 var(--font-display);
		letter-spacing: -0.035em;
		overflow-wrap: break-word;
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.sub {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 40rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}
	.headline :global(.pause) {
		position: absolute;
		left: calc(6.6 * var(--fs) + 8px);
		bottom: calc(0.14 * var(--fs));
	}
	/* Sorting as four stops on one line: the file's name changes from the first stop to the last. */
	.flow {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 20px;
		margin: 16px 0 4px;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.flow li {
		position: relative;
		display: grid;
		align-content: start;
		gap: 8px;
		padding-top: 22px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
	}
	.flow li::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: -4px;
		left: 0;
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--accent);
	}
	.flow .step {
		font: 500 1.25rem / 1.1 var(--font-display);
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.flow code {
		justify-self: start;
		max-width: 100%;
		padding: 2px 6px;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--chip);
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.flow li:last-child code {
		background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent), transparent 80%);
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.flow p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: var(--t-small);
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.paste {
		margin: 8px 0 0;
		max-width: 40rem;
	}
	.paste pre {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 18px 20px;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--chip);
		overflow-x: auto;
		font: 0.8125rem / 1.75 var(--font-mono);
		color: var(--muted);
		white-space: pre;
	}
	.paste mark {
		background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent), transparent 82%);
		color: var(--ink);
		border-radius: 4px;
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent), transparent 82%);
	}
	.paste figcaption,
	.ramp figcaption {
		margin-top: 10px;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: var(--t-small);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.paste figcaption span {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	/* Doubling, drawn: one hairline lane per connection, and a bar as long as the speed it reached. */
	.ramp {
		margin: 24px 0 0;
		max-width: 40rem;
	}
	.ramp ol {
		display: grid;
		gap: 14px;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.ramp li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) 10.5rem;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 14px;
	}
	.ramp b {
		font: 500 1.75rem / 1 var(--font-display);
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.ramp .lanes {
		height: 34px;
		background: repeating-linear-gradient(
			180deg,
			var(--accent) 0 1.5px,
			transparent 1.5px calc(34px / var(--n))
		);
		transform-origin: left;
		transform: scaleX(var(--speed));
		transition: transform 900ms var(--ease-out);
	}
	.ramp.idle .lanes {
		transform: scaleX(0.02);
	}
	.ramp .rate {
		font: 500 var(--t-small) / 1.3 var(--font-text);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.ramp em {
		display: block;
		font-style: normal;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.ramp li:nth-child(2) .lanes {
		transition-delay: 160ms;
	}
	.ramp li:nth-child(3) .lanes {
		transition-delay: 320ms;
	}
	/* Benchmark numbers set as display type: the one place the page shouts. */
	.stats {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 28px 32px;
		margin: 36px 0 8px;
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.stats div {
		display: grid;
		align-content: start;
		gap: 8px;
		padding-top: 16px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
	}
	.stats dt {
		font: 500 clamp(3rem, 6.4vw, 6rem) / 0.95 var(--font-display);
		letter-spacing: -0.045em;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	.stats dt span {
		font-size: 0.42em;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.stats dd {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: var(--t-small);
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	/* Feature overview: five groups on one set of rules, two across, the last one full width. */
	.overview {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 32px;
		margin: 16px 0 8px;
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.overview section {
		display: grid;
		align-content: start;
		gap: 8px;
		padding-top: 16px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
	}
	.overview section:last-child:nth-child(odd) {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
	}
